title ALES150 — Lotus's stereo_top_tail: the top-and-tail trimmer carried into stereo, one bracket for both channels, bound to ALES148 by the length bracket and ALES149 by the outer-take bracket
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Recur lap. REMEMBER is 337KB with a giant living-edge line, so the true living edge is git: Season C, the Lotus creative suite (waymark ALES), last landed ALES149 stereo_split_silence. ALES149's own recommend named the ascending crux plainly: ALES98 (top_tail — trim only the leading and trailing silence, keep every interior pause) carried into stereo. Ascending mono-ALES order after ALES97 names ALES98; crux-first and Lindy-first agree — the stereo edit corner grows on the silence readers, and top-and-tail is the single most-used silence gesture in every recorder and DAW, the natural companion to the trimmer (ALES148) and splitter (ALES149) just landed.
think Studied the trio it stands between: mono top_tail (ALES98, segment then cut only leading and trailing silence, tail-first so the leading index stays valid), stereo_trim_silence (ALES148, the frame-walk with two monotonic per-channel cursors marking jointly-silent frames), and stereo_split_silence (ALES149, coalesce not-jointly-silent frames into takes). The stereo top-tail fuses them: ALES148's silence-intersection frame walk to decide jointly-silent per frame, then find the FIRST and LAST not-jointly-silent frame and cut only the leading and trailing jointly-silent runs — tail first, then head, both channels in lockstep.
think The wall is the same one ALES148 and ALES149 named: top-and-tailing each channel by its own silence would give the two speakers different lengths and tear the stereo image apart, because ALES147 proved the two channels segment independently. So the rung decides one bracket for both — keep the span from the first frame either speaker fills to the last, so the bracket is the UNION of the two speakers' outer content. The honest bindings are two: the length bracket (stereo_trim_silence.len <= stereo_top_tail.len <= original.len, top-tail keeping every jointly-not-silent sample the trim keeps PLUS the interior joint-silences) and the outer-take bracket (the result equals ALES149's stereo split first-take-start to last-take-end byte for byte).
think Implementation: stereo_top_and_tail segments both channels up front through ALES147 (all validation, empty-clip BadFrame → both channels untouched), then one forward pass advances a cursor per channel across its tiling run list, marks each frame jointly-silent only where both are .silent, and records first_ns/last_ns; if none found the whole master is joint-silence, cut whole from both leaving each empty; else cut the trailing joint-silence first through ALES2 cut then the leading, the in-bounds span asserted before each cut so neither can fault and leave the pair half-trimmed, postcondition asserting both hold [first.start, last.end) and leave balanced. The stereo span law is proven against a second independent by-hand reference (frame verdicts by run scan, first/last by hand) across eight frame lengths, four floors, three splits.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. First-try witness GREEN, no red this round. Recorded lesson: when a mono length-changing edit brackets by its own silence (top-and-tail keeps the outer non-silent span), the stereo lift brackets by the UNION of the two speakers' outer content — the first-to-last not-jointly-silent frame — not by either channel alone, so the two stay balanced; the lockstep law makes this concrete (mono top_tail per channel desyncs to 12 and 4 where the stereo holds both at 16). Witness GREEN (four laws: stereo span, bracket, preservation/lockstep, degenerate/atomicity), width-check exit 0, my module carries dense asserts (not on the zero-assert ratchet). Front door lotus/README.md synced (ALES150 roster entry appended to the Status line).
loom witness=ales_stereo_top_tail_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=stereo-edit read=reads-through-segmenter+edits-in-lockstep form=bracket-first-to-last-not-joint decision=silence-intersection-at-ends cases=stereo-span-law(8flen*4floor*3split)+bracket-law(=ALES149-outer-takes,ALES148-trim<=len<=original)+preservation-lockstep(interior-joint-silent-kept,mono-per-channel-desync-12-and-4,stereo-16)+degenerate(all-joint-empty,no-joint-unchanged,head-only,tail-only)+atomicity(empty,ragged,inverted-band,illegal-floor) reds=0
file lotus/stereo_top_tail.rye ALES150 — stereo_top_tail, the top-and-tail trimmer lifted to stereo: cut only the leading and trailing joint silence, keep every interior pause, the kept span the union of the two speakers' outer content cut identically from both channels in lockstep (tail first); stereo_top_and_tail, StereoTopTailError = StereoSegmentError || EditError reused whole; bound to ALES148 by the length bracket and ALES149 by the outer-take bracket.
file tools/ales_stereo_top_tail_witness.rish the witness — three-say (Language/Style/Lens), builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-top-tail line.
